values ('d1f4b8a2-7c39-4e05-9b16-3a8e0c5d2f74', 'mental-health-nursing', 'Mental Health Nursing', 'This course develops the knowledge, skills, and professional stance needed for safe psychiatric-mental health nursing. Students learn therapeutic communication, psychiatric assessment, mental status examination, milieu care, trauma-informed practice, common psychiatric disorders, psychopharmacology, suicide and violence risk assessment, crisis intervention, substance use care, legal protections, and recovery-oriented transitions. The course emphasizes dignity, least-restrictive care, cultural humility, collaborative safety planning, integrated behavioral health, and simulation-based clinical judgment.');

